          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fermion"} fermion
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+particles"} fundamental particles
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            arrange in three “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generation+of+fundamental+particles"}> generations
            ”. Between generations, particles differ in their
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mass"} mass
            and in further properties referred to as
            = succeed "," do
              %em flavor quantum numbers
            %em flavor physics
            refers to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/phenomenology"} phenomenology
            of processes that do involve or depend on flavor quantum numbers, notably when flavor changes through interactions via the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+nuclear+force"} weak nuclear force
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yukawa+interactions"} Yukawa interactions
          %p
            For the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/leptons"} leptons
            these flavor quantum numbers are
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/electron"} electron
                number
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/muon"} muon
              number
            and
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tauon"} tauon
              number
            as well as the corresponding three
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrino"} neutrino
                numbers
          %p
            For the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            the flavor quantum numbers are
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isospin"} isospin
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/charm+quark"} charm
            = succeed "," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/strange+quark"}> strange
                \-ness
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom+quark"}> bottom
              \-ness
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/top+quark"}> top
                \-ness
          %p
            See
            %a{:href => "#yotams"} yotams
            for a good quick introduction.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#TheFlavorProblem The flavor problem
          %p
            In the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"} flavor physics
            – hence the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+boson"} Higgs boson
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interaction"} interaction
            with the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/generations+of+fermions"} generations of fermions
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yukawa+coupling"} Yukawa coupling
            = succeed "-sector" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CKM+matrix"} CKM matrix
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Lagrangian+density"} Lagrangian density
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Einstein-Yang-Mills-Dirac-Higgs+theory"} Einstein-Yang-Mills-Dirac-Higgs theory
            that defines the standard model – has some striking characteristics different from the sector that does not:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AltmannshoferFlavorSector.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              slide grabbed from
              %a{:href => "spring"} Altmannshofer 14
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/IsidoriFlavorSector.jpg", :width => "700"}/
          %blockquote
            %p
              slide grabbed from
              %a{:href => "#Isidori16"} Isidori 16
          %p
            (Note that Isidori’s slide collects all terms with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Higgs+boson"} Higgs boson
            factor, including the pure Higgs terms reflecting the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmological+constant"} cosmological constant
            and the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hierarchy+problem"} hierarchy problem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quark"} quark
            factors.)
          %p
            Broadly,
            %em the flavor problem
            (see the references
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#ReferencesFlavorProblem"} below
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/GUT"} GUT
            models and/or the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fine-tuning"} fine-tuning
            in the flavor sector.
          %p
            Moreover, all observed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CP+violation"} CP violation
            is related to flavor-changing
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interactions"} interactions
          %p
            Finally, due to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/confinement"} confinement
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            are not seen in isolation by collider
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiments"} experiments
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mesons"} mesons
            and/or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryons"} baryons
            that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quarks"} quarks
            are
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bound+state"} bound
            in. This way the flavor problem is tied to the
            %a{:href => "confinement#OpenProblem"} confinement problem
            and hence to the problem of formulating
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/non-perturbative+quantum+field+theory"} non-perturbatively
            (e.g. via
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} AdS/QCD
          %p All this suggests that the flavor sector is controlled by mechanisms that are not understood or identified yet.
          %h3#experimental_anomalies Experimental “anomalies”
          %p
            Due to the
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#TheFlavorProblem"} flavor problem
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model of particle physics
            is the least well understood in detail. Indeed, thete are persistent and growing discrepancies between SM-predictions and experimental measurements in the flavor sector:
          %h4#flavor_anomaly Flavor anomaly
          %p
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+anomalies"} flavor anomalies
            reflect a discrepancy in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/B-meson"} B-meson
            decays between
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/experiment"} experiment
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHCb"}> LHCb
            ,
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Belle+experiment"} Belle
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/BaBar+experiment"} BaBar
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/statistical+significance"} statistical significance
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ∼
                  %mn 4
                  %mi σ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sim 4\sigma
            across all experiments and decay channels. If these
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
            are real they signify New Physics in the flavor sector.
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
            for more.
          %h4#cabibbo_anomaly Cabibbo anomaly
          %p
            See at
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cabibbo+anomaly"} Cabibbo anomaly
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V_cb+puzzle"} V_cb puzzle
          %h4#_anomaly
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo −
                  %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (g-2)
            anomaly
          %p
            See at
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28g-2%29+anomaly"} (g-2) anomaly
          %h3#GeometircEngineeringInDBranes Geometric engineering on D8-branes
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+physics"} flavor physics
            in
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/open+strings"} open strings
            ending on
            = succeed "-filling" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/spacetime"} spacetime
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D-branes"} D-branes
            called “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+branes"}> flavor branes
            ” (
            %a{:href => "#KarchKatz02"}> Karch-Katz 02
            ).
          %p
            Specifically in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Sakai-Sugimoto model
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometrically engineering
            something close to actual
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+chromodynamics"} quantum chromodynamics
            (
            %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto04"}> Sakai-Sugimoto 04
            ,
            = succeed ")," do
              %a{:href => "#SakaiSugimoto05"} Sakai-Sugimoto 05
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
            in the model:
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/WSSBraneConfigurationEngineeringQCDII.jpg", :width => "740"}/
          %div{:style => "float:right;margin:0 10px 10px 0;"}
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/D8D6NS5.jpg", :width => "380"}/
          %p Here we are showing
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+%28particle+physics%29"} flavor
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
              %p with
              %ol
                %li
                  %p
                    the
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/5d+Chern-Simons+theory"} 5d Chern-Simons theory
                    on their
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/worldvolume"} worldvolume
                %li
                  %p
                    the corresponding
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4d+WZW+model"} 4d WZW model
                    on the boundary
              %p
                both exhibiting the
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meson+fields"} meson fields
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/baryon"} baryon
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D4-branes"} D4-branes
              %p
                (see at
                = succeed ");" do
                  %em
                    %a{:href => "WSS+model#Baryons"} WSS-model – Baryons
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yang-Mills+monopole"} Yang-Mills monopole
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-branes"} D6-branes
              %p
                (see at
                = succeed ");" do
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D6-D8-brane+bound+state"} D6-D8-brane bound state
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/NS5-branes"} NS5-branes
                (often not considered here).
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/light+and+heavy+flavor"} light and heavy flavor
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CKM+matrix"} CKM matrix
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yukawa+coupling"} Yukawa coupling
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/color+charge"} color charge
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomaly"} flavour anomaly
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cabibbo+anomaly"}> Cabibbo anomaly
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/V_cb+puzzle"} V_cb puzzle
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+brane"} flavor brane
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quantum+hadrodynamics"} quantum hadrodynamics
              %ul
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+supersymmetry"} hadron supersymmetry
                %li
                  %p
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/hadron+Kaluza-Klein+theory"} hadron Kaluza-Klein theory
          %h2#references References
          %h3#general General
          %p A good quick account:
          %ul
            %li#yotams
              yotams,
              %em What is flavor?
              (
              %a{:href => "https://webhome.weizmann.ac.il/home/yotams/notes/ep1_flavor.pdf"}> pdf
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/yotamsFlavor.pfd", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p Textbook accounts:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Robert+E.+Marshak"}> Robert E. Marshak
                , Chapter 3 of:
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Conceptual Foundations of Modern Particle Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/1767"} doi:10.1142/1767
            %li#Buras20
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrzej+Buras"}> Andrzej Buras
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Gauge Theory of Weak Decays
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1017/9781139524100"} doi:10.1017/9781139524100
                %a{:href => "https://cerncourier.com/a/the-hitchhikers-guide-to-weak-decays/"} CERN review
                by
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gino+Isidori"} Gino Isidori
          %p Lecture notes:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuval+Grossman"}> Yuval Grossman
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Introduction to flavor physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1006.3534"} arXiv:1006.3534
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benjamin+Grinstein"}> Benjamin Grinstein
                ,
                %em TASI-2013 Lectures on Flavor Physics
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1501.05283"}> arXiv:1501.05283
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuval+Grossman"}> Yuval Grossman
                , Philip Tanedo,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Just a Taste: Lectures on Flavor Physics
                %em Anticipating the Next Discoveries in Particle Physics (TASI 2016)
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1711.03624"}> arXiv:1711.03624
                ,
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1142/9789813233348_0004"} doi:10.1142/9789813233348_0004
            %li#Zupan19
              %p
                Jure Zupan,
                %em Introduction to flavour physics
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1903.05062"}> arXiv:1903.05062
                )
          %p
            With an emphasis on
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CP+violation"} CP violation
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Antonio+Pich"}> Antonio Pich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Flavour Dynamics and Violations of the CP Symmetry
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.08597"} arXiv:1805.08597
          %p
            With an emphasis on the
            = succeed "-sector:" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrino"} neutrino
          %ul
            %li
              Zhi-zhong Xing,
              %em Flavor structures of charged fermions and massive neutrinos
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.09610"}> arXiv:1909.09610
              )
          %p
            Beyond the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/standard+model+of+particle+physics"} standard model
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Altmannshofer"}> Wolfgang Altmannshofer
              ,
              = succeed ":" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Peter+Stangl"} Peter Stangl
              %em Flavour Physics Beyond the Standard Model
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.03950"}> arXiv:2508.03950
              \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Wikipedia,
                %a{:href => "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flavour_(particle_physics)"} Flavour (particle physcs)
            %li
              %p
                Fernando Abreu de Souza, Gero von Gersdorff,
                %em A Random Clockwork of Flavor
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1911.08476"}> arxiv:1911.08476
                )
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+physics"} flavour physics
            and
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
            seen at the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHCb+experiment"} LHCb experiment
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Niels+Tuning"}> Niels Tuning
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Recent results from LHCb
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.nikhef.nl/event/2253"} nikhef event:2253
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.nikhef.nl/event/2253/material/slides/0.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/TuningFlavourAnomaly20.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              %blockquote
                %p In recent years a number of results in flavour physics have drawn some attention due to tensions with respect to Standard Model predictions. An overview of these results will be shown, together with a few recent results from this Spring, both on the flavour anomalies and ‘classical’ flavour physics
          %p Survey and outlook:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riccardo+Barbieri"}> Riccardo Barbieri
                ,
                %em A view of flavour physics in 2021
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2103.15635"}> arXiv:2103.15635
                )
            %li
              %p
                Vladimir V. Gligorov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Overview of quark flavour results
                %a{:href => "https://www.ichep2022.it/"} ICHEP 2022
                (Bologna, 2022) &amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://agenda.infn.it/event/28874/contributions/171923/"}> infn:171923
                ,
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://agenda.infn.it/event/28874/contributions/171923/attachments/94847/130108/Vladimir_Gligorov.pdf"} pdf
          %h3#ReferencesFlavorProblem The flavour problem
          %p
            On the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+problem"} flavour problem
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gino+Isidori"}> Gino Isidori
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Kaon decays and the flavour problem
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-ph/0301159"} arXiv:hep-ph/0301159
              %p
                (emphasis on
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kaon"} kaon
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering"} decays
            %li#Isidori16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gino+Isidori"}> Gino Isidori
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The flavor problem
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/504502/contributions/2147710/attachments/1287372/1915547/SWHEPPS_Talk.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/IsidoriFlavor16.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
            %li#Altmannshofer14
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Wolfgang+Altmannshofer"}> Wolfgang Altmannshofer
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Flavor Puzzle
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.aspenphys.org/science/colloquia/2014_slides/altmannshofer.pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/AltmannshoferFlavorProblem.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
          %p
            In relation to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/neutrino+mass+problem"} neutrino mass problem
          %ul
            %li#Xing19
              Zhi-zhong Xing,
              %em Flavor structures of charged fermions and massive neutrinos
              Physics Reports Volume 854, 20 April 2020, Pages 1-147 (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.09610"}> arXiv:1909.09610
              ,
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.physrep.2020.02.001"} doi:10.1016/j.physrep.2020.02.001
          %p
            On the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+problem"} flavor problem
            in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MSSM"} MSSM
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Stuart+Raby"}> Stuart Raby
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em SUSY Flavor Problem
              = succeed "." do
                %em Supersymmetric Grand Unified Theories
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/978-3-319-55255-2_7"} doi:10.1007/978-3-319-55255-2_7
          %h3#flavour_anomalies Flavour anomalies
          %p
            Outlook on the field of flavour physics in view of
            = succeed "-measurement" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/LHCb"} LHCb
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
            and
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CP+violation"} CP violation
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Benjamin+Grinstein"}> Benjamin Grinstein
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A path to flavor
                %em
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/769902/"} Implications of LHCb measurement and future prospects
                CERN 2019 (
                %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/769902/contributions/3582540/attachments/1926501/3193107/Grinstein-high-res.pdf"}> pdf
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/GrinsteinFlavor2019.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/769902/contributions/3582540"} indico:3582540
            %li
              %p
                Monika Blanke,
                %em Flavour Physics from Present to Future Colliders
                (
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1910.10662"}> arxiv:1910.10662
                )
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li#AHRS20
              Rafael Aoude, Tobias Hurth, Sophie Renner, William Shepherd,
              %em The impact of flavour data on global fits of the MFV SMEFT
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2003.05432"}> arXiv:2003.05432
              )
          %p
            On
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+physics"} flavour physics
            and potential
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavour+anomalies"} flavour anomalies
            in
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/kaon"} kaon
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/scattering"} decays
          %ul
            %li#Buras16
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrzej+Buras"}> Andrzej Buras
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Revival of Kaon Flavour Physics
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1609.05711"} arXiv:1609.05711
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1051/epjconf/201612900050"} doi:10.1051/epjconf/201612900050
            %li#Buras18
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrzej+Buras"}> Andrzej Buras
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em The Return of Kaon Flavour Physics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://www.actaphys.uj.edu.pl/index_n.php?I=R&V=49&N=6#1043"} doi:10.5506/APhysPolB.49.1043
          %h3#geometric_engineering_on_flavor_branes Geometric engineering on flavor branes
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/geometric+engineering+of+QFT"} geometric engineering
            of flavour physics in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersecting+D-brane+models"} intersecting D-brane models
            (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+branes"} flavor branes
            in
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AdS%2FQCD"} AdS/QCD
          %ul
            %li#KarchKatz02
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andreas+Karch"}> Andreas Karch
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Emanuel+Katz"} Emanuel Katz
              = succeed "," do
                %em Adding flavor to AdS/CFT
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0205236"} arxiv:hep-th/0205236
          %p
            and then developed in detail for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/QCD"} QCD
            on
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D8-branes"} D8-branes
            in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sakai-Sugimoto+model"} Sakai-Sugimoto model
          %ul
            %li#SakaiSugimoto04
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadakatsu+Sakai"}> Tadakatsu Sakai
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"} Shigeki Sugimoto
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Low energy hadron physics in holographic QCD
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0412141"} arXiv:hep-th/0412141
            %li#SakaiSugimoto05
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tadakatsu+Sakai"}> Tadakatsu Sakai
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Shigeki+Sugimoto"} Shigeki Sugimoto
                = succeed "," do
                  %em More on a holographic dual of QCD
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/0507073"} arXiv:hep-th/0507073
          %div
            %h3#FlavorOnSingleHeteroticM5BranesReferences
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi SU
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)
              \-flavor symmetry on heterotic M5-branes
            %p
              Emergence of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/SU%282%29"} SU(2)
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/flavor+%28particle+physics%29"} flavor
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chiral+symmetry"} symmetry
              on single
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+M-theory+on+ADE-orbifolds"} heterotic M-theory on ADE-orbifolds
              (in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%281%2C0%29+SCFT"} D=6 N=(1,0) SCFT
              on
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/small+instantons"} small instantons
              in
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/heterotic+string+theory"} heterotic string theory
            %ul
              %li
                %p
